  "voiceRules": [
    "Address the person as “you.” Names are occasional human context, not a personalization badge on every page. Say what changes and what stays in ordinary training words. The sample user is Alex. Friendly means choice without judgment.",
    "Do not claim real coaching, microphone capture, a connected account, injury assessment, calories, body composition, or clinical personalization. Coach carries “Sample conversation” so review/apply actions have an honest scope. Inputs and local controls work; their effects are defined in page-contract.md.",
    "All foreground pairs meet 4.5:1 at normal size even when the role would permit 3:1. Interactive boundaries meet 3:1 against their adjacent surfaces. Increased Contrast uses the control-boundary token in place of the decorative divider and 2 pt for active boundaries. Reduce Transparency already matches the specified opaque UI. VoiceOver order follows top-to-bottom rows; expose a station's position, exercise, status and prescription as one coherent item, with actions separately reachable. Charts provide the same data as text. Focus returns to the invoking control after a sheet is dismissed. Announce an applied change and an explicit set confirmation once.",
    "Only numeric fields use numeric/decimal keyboards. Their labels and units remain visible outside the field. A locale's decimal input must not be silently dropped; for this English fixture accept 12, 12.5, or 12,5 and normalize only after validation. Empty, negative, nonnumeric, or out-of-range values get a linked error and preserve the user's input. Limits here are demo input constraints, not clinical advice."
  ],
  "doDont": [
    "Do: keep one blue action per surface; spell out units (\"3 sets of 8–10 reps\", \"12 kg\"); keep status in words; let rows grow.",
    "Do: keep the rail aligned across every ordered list; put numbers in Barlow and everything you read in Atkinson.",
    "Don't: tint rows blue, add shadows/gradients/glass on content, ellipsize names, use tracked caps, animate numbers, or imply real coaching, cloud save or health claims."
  ],
  "accessibility": [
    "Native tab bar and navigation stacks: use real tab semantics; if the native container imposes iOS 26 glass on the tab bar, record it and validate contrast instead of drawing a second layer.",
    "Status bar, Dynamic Island and home indicator are simulated drawings (Atkinson Bold stands in for SF Pro 9:41); the device draws the real ones. Do not implement them.",
    "Sheets: use native sheet presentation with detents sized to content, native grabber and swipe-to-dismiss; the drawn grabber is an approximation.",
    "Keyboard: numeric keypad for repetitions, decimal keypad for weight; the composer rises above the keyboard; focused input scrolls into view.",
    "Haptics: one light success haptic on Finish, Apply and Move commits only; none on failure or no-op.",
    "Spring feel for sheets (critically damped 0.35 s) cannot be shown in HTML.",
    "Dynamic Type: scale every text role by its mapped iOS style (tokens dynamicType.accessibilityLarge shows AX2); tab labels use the large-content viewer instead of scaling.",
    "VoiceOver: rows are single elements with the composed labels in the source (aria-label); rail numerals and bar graphics are hidden; announcements listed in interactions.",
    "Increase Contrast: replace divider with border.control and use 2 pt active boundaries.",
    "Reduce Motion: filing becomes a 120 ms crossfade; chevrons and bars change instantly."
  ],
