  "transitions": [
    "today → workout: Review workout / Continue workout (navigation only; nothing starts or records). Return: Workout's \"Back to Today\" or the Today tab.",
    "today → plan: Wednesday or Friday week row selects that day. Return: Today tab.",
    "today → progress: Monday row or \"Review your session\" opens the sessions sheet with that session expanded. Return: Close / swipe down, then Today tab.",
    "plan → move sheet: Move session (blocked with a notice when the workout has recorded sets). Sheet: choose Thursday or Saturday → \"Move to Thursday\" commits; Cancel / Close / swipe leaves the week unchanged. After commit: \"Session moved to Thursday.\" with Undo move.",
    "plan rest day: \"Move Wednesday here\" (Thursday or Saturday only, when eligible) commits the same move with Undo.",
    "plan → recorded sheet: Monday → Review recorded sets. Close returns.",
    "plan → workout: dock Review workout (pending session only).",
    "workout ready → active: Start workout (zero records). active: steppers/inputs edit a draft; Confirm set validates and records one set ID once → notice with Undo set → Next set / Next exercise / Review workout. Finish (header) or final Review workout → finish sheet.",
    "finish sheet: ≥1 record → \"Finish and keep N sets\" files the session (partial or full) → summary with dock Back to Today; \"Keep working\" / Close keeps everything. 0 records → \"Return to workout\" or \"End without recording\" (adds nothing).",
    "coach → plan-review sheet: Review shorter plan. \"Use this plan\" applies once (Today/Plan/Workout show 20 min / 3 exercises / 7 planned sets); \"Keep current plan\" / Close changes nothing. Applied → Undo change restores the exact snapshot.",
    "coach composer: Send (disabled for whitespace) adds your text and a deterministic sample reply; prompts \"Why these exercises?\" and \"Keep the full session\" add fixed replies. No reply commits a plan.",
    "progress: Sets/Sessions switches values and units together; tapping a week selects it; Review sessions opens the week's sessions sheet; tapping a session expands its sets inside the sheet."
  ],
